requirement declaration.\", \"Separate business behavior tests from adapter/infrastructure contract tests.\", \"Use JUnit Jupiter and plain Mockito mock/when/verify calls; no experimental JVM compatibility flags.\", \"Mock external interfaces instead of generating handwritten implementations.\", \"Prefer narrow generated collaborators; do not change accepted production APIs just for tests.\", \"Preserve meaningful assertions and derive expectations from evidence, not from the example values.\"], \"examples\": [{\"path\": \"AdapterContractTest.java\", \"content\": \"package example;\\n\\nimport java.sql.CallableStatement;\\nimport java.sql.Connection;\\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;\\nimport static org.mockito.Mockito.*;\\n\\n/** Infrastructure contract example: no database connection or handwritten JDBC implementation. */\\npublic class AdapterContractTest {\\n    @Test void adapterPassesTheIdentifierToItsDependency() throws Exception {\\n        Connection connection = mock(Connection.class);\\n        CallableStatement statement = mock(CallableStatement.class);\\n        when(connection.prepareCall(\\\"{call sample(?)}\\\")).thenReturn(statement);\\n        when(statement.getString(1)).thenReturn(\\\"sample-result\\\");\\n        try (CallableStatement call = connection.prepareCall(\\\"{call sample(?)}\\\")) {\\n            call.setString(1, \\\"sample-id\\\");\\n            call.execute();\\n            assertEquals(\\\"sample-result\\\", call.getString(1));\\n        }\\n        verify(statement).setString(1, \\\"sample-id\\\");\\n        verify(statement).execute();\\n        verify(statement).close();\\n    }\\n}\\n\"}, {\"path\": \"BusinessBehaviorTest.java\", \"content\": \"package example;\\n\\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;\\nimport static org.mockito.Mockito.*;\\n\\n/** Reference structure only: derive real expected values from migration evidence. */\\npublic class BusinessBehaviorTest {\\n    interface NotificationPort { void send(String reference); }\\n    static class CompletionService {\\n        private final NotificationPort notifications;\\n        CompletionService(NotificationPort notifications) { this.notifications = notifications; }\\n        String complete(String reference) { notifications.send(reference); return reference; }\\n    }\\n\\n    @Test void returnsTheCompletedReference() {\\n        NotificationPort notifications = mock(NotificationPort.class);\\n        CompletionService service = new CompletionService(notifications);\\n        assertEquals(\\\"sample-reference\\\", service.complete(\\\"sample-reference\\\"));\\n    }\\n\\n    @Test void notifiesTheCollaboratorOnce() {\\n        NotificationPort notifications = mock(NotificationPort.class);\\n        new CompletionService(notifications).complete(\\\"sample-reference\\\");\\n        verify(notifications).send(\\\"sample-reference\\\");\\n        verifyNoMoreInteractions(notifications);\\n    }\\n}\\n\"}]}, \"final_validation_feedback\": null, \"method_contract_validation\": \"resolved-java-types-v1\", \"generic_method_validation\": \"erased-type-arguments-v1\", \"dependency_validation\": \"resolved-class-ownership-v1\", \"transitive_class_validation\": \"resolved-transitive-api-v1\", \"source_comment_validation\": \"comments-ignored-v1\", \"versioned_requirements\": [{\"requirement_id\": \"business\", \"version\": 1, \"description\": \"Preserve this complete configured unit's evidenced behavior\"}, {\"requirement_id\": \"java25-test-template\", \"version\": 1, \"description\": \"Use the verified Java 25 JUnit/Mockito testing platform with small focused behavior tests and separate adapter contract tests; mock external interfaces rather than hand implement them.\"}], \"schema\": {\"$defs\": {\"MavenDependency\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Identify a pinned Maven artifact and the APIs that justify its inclusion.\", \"properties\": {\"group_id\": {\"pattern\": \"^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*$\", \"title\": \"Group Id\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"artifact_id\": {\"pattern\": \"^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*$\", \"title\": \"Artifact Id\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"version\": {\"pattern\": \"^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*$\", \"title\": \"Version\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"scope\": {\"default\": \"compile\", \"enum\": [\"compile\", \"runtime\", \"provided\", \"test\"], \"title\": \"Scope\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"title\": \"Reason\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"required_classes\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Required Classes\", \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"group_id\", \"artifact_id\", \"version\", \"reason\"], \"title\": \"MavenDependency\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"NativeApiContract\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"A planned native type and exact public methods it must expose.\", \"properties\": {\"type_name\": {\"title\": \"Type Name\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"method_signatures\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Method Signatures\", \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"type_name\"], \"title\": \"NativeApiContract\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"NativeSourceFile\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"One text Java source under a safe Maven source directory.\", \"properties\": {\"path\": {\"title\": \"Path\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"content\": {\"title\": \"Content\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"path\", \"content\"], \"title\": \"NativeSourceFile\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"OperationDataContract\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Reconciled explicit Java data types and all configured-unit interfaces.\", \"properties\": {\"sources\": {\"items\": {\"additionalProperties\": true, \"type\": \"object\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"title\": \"Sources\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"units\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/UnitContract\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"title\": \"Units\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"service_api\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NativeApiContract\"}, \"request_type\": {\"title\": \"Request Type\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"success_type\": {\"title\": \"Success Type\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"error_type\": {\"title\": \"Error Type\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"request_wire_type\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Request Wire Type\"}, \"success_wire_type\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Success Wire Type\"}, \"error_wire_type\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Error Wire Type\"}, \"service_requirements\": {\"additionalProperties\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Service Requirements\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"step_dependencies\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/OperationDependency\"}, \"title\": \"Step Dependencies\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"runtime_resources\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/OperationResource\"}, \"title\": \"Runtime Resources\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"unresolved_questions\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Unresolved Questions\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"schema_version\": {\"default\": \"v1\", \"title\": \"Schema Version\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"sources\", \"units\", \"service_api\", \"request_type\", \"success_type\", \"error_type\"], \"title\": \"OperationDataContract\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"OperationDependency\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Bind a configured step to a typed constructor argument and service field.\", \"properties\": {\"binding_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"title\": \"Binding Id\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"unit_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"title\": \"Unit Id\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"type_name\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"title\": \"Type Name\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"parameter_name\": {\"pattern\": \"^[A-Za-z_$][\\\\w$]*$\", \"title\": \"Parameter Name\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"field_name\": {\"pattern\": \"^[A-Za-z_$][\\\\w$]*$\", \"title\": \"Field Name\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"binding_id\", \"unit_id\", \"type_name\", \"parameter_name\", \"field_name\"], \"title\": \"OperationDependency\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"OperationResource\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Describe a configured provider and the input value it creates per execution.\", \"properties\": {\"input_key\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"title\": \"Input Key\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"resource_type\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"title\": \"Resource Type\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"provider_type\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"title\": \"Provider Type\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"parameter_name\": {\"pattern\": \"^[A-Za-z_$][\\\\w$]*$\", \"title\": \"Parameter Name\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"field_name\": {\"pattern\": \"^[A-Za-z_$][\\\\w$]*$\", \"title\": \"Field Name\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"connection_id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Connection Id\"}, \"transaction_scope\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Transaction Scope\"}}, \"required\": [\"input_key\", \"resource_type\", \"provider_type\", \"parameter_name\", \"field_name\"], \"title\": \"OperationResource\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"UnitContract\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Required APIs, dependencies and evidence-backed requirements for a unit.\", \"properties\": {\"unit_id\": {\"title\": \"Unit Id\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"apis\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NativeApiContract\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"title\": \"Apis\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"dependency_units\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Dependency Units\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"requirements\": {\"additionalProperties\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minProperties\": 1, \"title\": \"Requirements\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"evidence_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"title\": \"Evidence Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"unit_id\", \"apis\", \"requirements\", \"evidence_ids\"], \"title\": \"UnitContract\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Candidate native implementation with test and requirement evidence.\", \"properties\": {\"files\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/NativeSourceFile\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"title\": \"Files\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"dependencies\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/MavenDependency\"}, \"title\": \"Dependencies\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"coverage\": {\"additionalProperties\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"title\": \"Coverage\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"evidence_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Evidence Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"unresolved_questions\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Unresolved Questions\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"unit_contract\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/UnitContract\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"input_type\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Input Type\"}, \"output_type\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Output Type\"}, \"wire_type\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Wire Type\"}, \"operation_contract\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/OperationDataContract\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"schema_version\": {\"default\": \"v1\", \"title\": \"Schema Version\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"files\"], \"title\": \"NativeUnitBundle\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"previous_model_response\": \"{\\\"files\\\": [{\\\"path\\\": \\\"src/main/java/com/company/generated/units/u3a42c4326e3d/MapErrorByValueAlways.java\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"package com.company.generated.units.u3a42c4326e3d;\\\\n\\\\nimport com.ibm.dse.base.CCOperationStep;\\\\nimport com.ibm.dse.base.Context;\\\\n\\\\npublic class MapErrorByValueAlways extends CCOperationStep {\\\\n    private String errorCategory = \\\\\\\"99\\\\\\\";\\\\n    private String errorNumber = \\\\\\\"8\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n    public void setErrorCategory(String errorCategory) {\\\\n        this.errorCategory = errorCategory;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    public void setErrorNumber(String errorNumber) {\\\\n        this.errorNumber = errorNumber;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    @Override\\\\n    public int execute() throws Exception {\\\\n        Context ctx = getContext();\\\\n        ctx.setValueAt(\\\\\\\"ErrorCategory\\\\\\\", errorCategory);\\\\n        ctx.setValueAt(\\\\\\\"ErrorNumber\\\\\\\", errorNumber);\\\\n        ctx.setValueAt(\\\\\\\"ErrorDescription\\\\\\\", resolveErrorDescription(errorCategory, errorNumber));\\\\n        return 0;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    private String resolveErrorDescription(String category, String number) {\\\\n        String key = category + \\\\\\\"_\\\\\\\" + number;\\\\n        switch (key) {\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"10_2\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"Validation failed: required field missing or invalid\\\\\\\";\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"20_1\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"No data found for the provided criteria\\\\\\\";\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"20_4\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"Account not found\\\\\\\";\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"30_5\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"Access denied: insufficient permissions\\\\\\\";\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"40_3\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"Daily transfer limit exceeded\\\\\\\";\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"40_4\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"Insufficient funds\\\\\\\";\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"40_5\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"Account not eligible for this operation\\\\\\\";\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"50_2\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"Transfer blocked: fraud risk detected\\\\\\\";\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"60_6\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"Core banking system rejected the request\\\\\\\";\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"60_7\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"Transfer already processed\\\\\\\";\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"99_0\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"Technical error: unexpected system failure\\\\\\\";\\\\n            case \\\\\\\"99_8\\\\\\\": return \\\\\\\"Technical error: database connection failure\\\\\\\";\\\\n            default:     return \\\\\\\"System error (category=\\\\\\\" + category + \\\\\\\", number=\\\\\\\" + number + \\\\\\\")\\\\\\\";\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"path\\\": \\\"src/test/java/com/company/generated/units/u3a42c4326e3d/MapErrorByValueAlwaysTest.java\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"package com.company.generated.units.u3a42c4326e3d;\\\\n\\\\nimport com.ibm.dse.base.Context;\\\\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\\\\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;\\\\n\\\\npublic class MapErrorByValueAlwaysTest {\\\\n\\\\n    @Test\\\\n    public void executesAndSetsConfiguredDatabaseError() throws Exception {\\\\n        Context context = new Context();\\\\n        MapErrorByValueAlways step = new MapErrorByValueAlways();\\\\n        step.setContext(context);\\\\n        \\\\n        int result = step.execute();\\\\n        \\\\n        assertEquals(0, result);\\\\n        assertEquals(\\\\\\\"99\\\\\\\", context.getValueAt(\\\\\\\"ErrorCategory\\\\\\\"));\\\\n        assertEquals(\\\\\\\"8\\\\\\\", context.getValueAt(\\\\\\\"ErrorNumber\\\\\\\"));\\\\n        assertEquals(\\\\\\\"Technical error: database connection failure\\\\\\\", context.getValueAt(\\\\\\\"ErrorDescription\\\\\\\"));\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    @Test\\\\n    public void executesWithCustomErrorValues() throws Exception {\\\\n        Context context = new Context();\\\\n        MapErrorByValueAlways step = new MapErrorByValueAlways();\\\\n        step.setContext(context);\\\\n        step.setErrorCategory(\\\\\\\"10\\\\\\\");\\\\n        step.setErrorNumber(\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\");\\\\n        \\\\n        int result = step.execute();\\\\n        \\\\n        assertEquals(0, result);\\\\n        assertEquals(\\\\\\\"10\\\\\\\", context.getValueAt(\\\\\\\"ErrorCategory\\\\\\\"));\\\\n        assertEquals(\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\", context.getValueAt(\\\\\\\"ErrorNumber\\\\\\\"));\\\\n        assertEquals(\\\\\\\"Validation failed: required field missing or invalid\\\\\\\", context.getValueAt(\\\\\\\"ErrorDescription\\\\\\\"));\\\\n    }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\"}], \\\"dependencies\\\": [{\\\"group_id\\\": \\\"org.junit.jupiter\\\", \\\"artifact_id\\\": \\\"junit-jupiter\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"5.10.0\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"test\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"JUnit Jupiter tests and execution engine\\\", \\\"required_classes\\\": [\\\"org.junit.jupiter.api.Test\\\", \\\"org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions\\\"]}, {\\\"group_id\\\": \\\"org.mockito\\\", \\\"artifact_id\\\": \\\"mockito-core\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"5.23.0\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"test\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Mockito mocking framework\\\", \\\"required_classes\\\": []}, {\\\"group_id\\\": \\\"net.bytebuddy\\\", \\\"artifact_id\\\": \\\"byte-buddy\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.17.7\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"test\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"ByteBuddy dependency for Mockito\\\", \\\"required_classes\\\": []}, {\\\"group_id\\\": \\\"net.bytebuddy\\\", \\\"artifact_id\\\": \\\"byte-buddy-agent\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.17.7\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"test\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"ByteBuddy agent dependency for Mockito\\\", \\\"required_classes\\\": []}, {\\\"group_id\\\": \\\"org.objenesis\\\", \\\"artifact_id\\\": \\\"objenesis\\\", \\\"version\\\": \\\"3.3\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"test\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Objenesis dependency for Mockito\\\", \\\"required_classes\\\": []}], \\\"coverage\\\": {\\\"business\\\": [\\\"src/test/java/com/company/generated/units/u3a42c4326e3d/MapErrorByValueAlwaysTest.java\\\"]}, \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"configured_step-3a42c4326e3d7f21467b61b2\\\", \\\"com.ibm.il.dse.operations.common.MapErrorByValueAlways\\\"], \\\"unresolved_questions\\\": [], \\\"input_type\\\": null, \\\"output_type\\\": null, \\\"wire_type\\\": null, \\\"operation_contract\\\": null, \\\"unit_contract\\\": {\\\"unit_id\\\": \\\"configured_step-3a42c4326e3d7f21467b61b2\\\", \\\"apis\\\": [{\\\"type_name\\\": \\\"com.company.generated.units.u3a42c4326e3d.MapErrorByValueAlways\\\", \\\"method_signatures\\\": [\\\"public int execute() throws java.lang.Exception\\\", \\\"public void setErrorCategory(java.lang.String)\\\", \\\"public void setErrorNumber(java.lang.String)\\\"]}], \\\"dependency_units\\\": [], \\\"requirements\\\": {\\\"business\\\": \\\"Preserve this complete configured unit's evidenced behavior\\\"}, \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\\"configured_step-3a42c4326e3d7f21467b61b2\\\", \\\"com.ibm.il.dse.operations.common.MapErrorByValueAlways\\\"]}, \\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"v1\\\"}\", \"correction_feedback\": \"Prohibited framework dependency in src/main/java/com/company/generated/units/u3a42c4326e3d/MapErrorByValueAlways.java (type com.company.generated.units.u3a42c4326e3d.MapErrorByValueAlways): com.ibm.dse.base.CCOperationStep; com.ibm.dse.base.Context. Remove these imports/references from implementation and tests. If the unit needs this supporting behavior, include a native companion implementation derived from the supplied supporting source evidence and wire its callers, public API metadata and tests to that returned type. Reuse an accepted native API if supplied; retain ordinary external APIs only through declared dependencies. Do not invent a migrated package, restore an IBM import, or supply only an interface/mock for required production behavior. Use typed inputs/results for steps and Jackson wire models with plain mapper transformations for formats; do not recreate a Composer runtime.\", \"composer_behavior_evidence\": [{\"document\": \"embedded:composer_conversion_knowledge\", \"heading\": \"4. Runtime Execution Model\", \"content\": \"## 4. Runtime Execution Model\\n\\n### High-Level Flow\\n\\nWhen a channel handler receives an HTTP/service request for operation `GetClientLinksOp`:\\n\\n```\\n1. Channel Handler receives request XML\\n2. Looks up \\\"GetClientLinksOp\\\" in dse.ini selfDefOper → finds XML file path\\n3. Loads and initializes CCDSEServerOperation from that XML file\\n4. Channel Handler calls: operation.unformat(requestXml)\\n   → request format cascades through the fmtDef structure\\n   → each formatter tag reads its value from the XML and writes it to context\\n   → each decorator in the chain transforms the value before/after the formatter\\n5. Channel Handler calls: operation.execute()\\n   → opStep chain runs according to RC routing\\n   → opSteps read from / write to context\\n6. Channel Handler calls: operation.format()\\n   → response format cascades through the reply fmtDef\\n   → each formatter tag reads its value from context and builds XML output\\n   → each decorator transforms the value\\n7. Channel Handler returns the formatted XML response\\n```\\n\\n**Important:** Steps 4, 5, and 6 are managed by the channel handler infrastructure. The developer defines what happens inside each step, not the orchestration between them.\\n\\n### CCDSEServerOperation.execute() — The opStep Loop\\n\\nThe execute() method runs the opStep chain:\\n\\n```java\\n// Pseudocode of CCDSEServerOperation.execute()\\npublic void execute() throws Exception {\\n    // 1. Set channel context values\\n    setValueAt(\\\"HOST_HEADER.HOST_KEY\\\", getHostKey());\\n    setFields(getOperationfields());\\n\\n    // 2. Filter opSteps not applicable to this channel\\n    removeOpStepsNotForThisChannel();\\n\\n    // 3. Run the opStep chain\\n    int index = 0;\\n    KeyedCollection end_opstep = null;\\n    if (isFinallyOpStepExist()) {\\n        end_opstep = getFinallyOpStep();  // the \\\"End\\\" step if defined\\n    }\\n\\n    do {\\n        KeyedCollection kc = getOperationStep(index);\\n        index = processOpStep(kc, operationName, index);\\n    } while (index != -1);\\n\\n    // 4. Run the \\\"End\\\" step if it exists\\n    if (end_opstep != null) {\\n        processOpStep(end_opstep, operationName, index);\\n    }\\n\\n    // 5. Error body substitution (if an opStep switched the reply format)\\n    if (isReturnedErrorBodyChanged() && getReturnedErrorBodyChanger() != null) {\\n        // substitute csErrorReplyFormat for csReplyFormat\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### processOpStep() — RC Routing\\n\\nThe RC routing priority for each opStep result:\\n\\n```\\n1. Check \\\"on{RC}Return\\\" → if set, switch the error reply format body\\n2. If RC == RC_TIMEOUT → check \\\"onTimeoutDo\\\" first\\n3. Check \\\"on{RC}Do\\\" → if found, go to that step name\\n4. Check \\\"onOtherDo\\\" → if found, go to that step name\\n5. Check \\\"onOtherDoDefault\\\" → if found, use it (with warning log)\\n6. If next == \\\"next\\\" → increment index, continue loop\\n7. If next == \\\"end\\\"  → return -1, break loop\\n8. Otherwise → look up step by name, jump to it\\n```\\n\\n### Channel Filtering — onlyFor\\n\\nBefore execute() runs, `removeOpStepsNotForThisChannel()` scans all opSteps and removes any that have an `onlyFor` attribute whose value does not match the current channel name.\\n\\n```xml\\n<!-- This step only runs on the INTERNET channel -->\\n<opStep id=\\\"InternetOnlyValidation\\\"\\n        implClass=\\\"operations.InternetValidation\\\"\\n        onlyFor=\\\"internet\\\"\\n        on0Do=\\\"end\\\"\\n        onOtherDo=\\\"OperationFailed\\\"/>\\n```\\n\\n**Conversion rule:** When converting an operation XML to native code for a specific channel, opSteps with `onlyFor` values that do not match the target channel are simply omitted from the generated code. The generated class reflects only the steps that actually run for that channel.\\n\\n---\", \"content_hash\": \"dee87849ddd2a8bf3ecb387db49b4302c23c852b54f4850643bb8f7c2bb63e4a\"}, {\"document\": \"embedded:composer_conversion_knowledge\", \"heading\": \"5. Context\", \"content\": \"## 5. Context\\n\\n### What Context Is\\n\\nThe context is a hierarchical runtime data store. It is the central communication mechanism between all components of an operation — formatters read from and write to it, opSteps read from and write to it, decorators do not directly access it (they transform string values, not context fields).\\n\\nAt runtime, the context is essentially a nested map:\\n```\\ncontext[\\\"ClientId\\\"]      = \\\"123456\\\"\\ncontext[\\\"ClientName\\\"]    = \\\"John Doe\\\"\\ncontext[\\\"links\\\"]         = [list of link objects]\\ncontext[\\\"ERROR_CODE\\\"]    = \\\"10\\\"\\ncontext[\\\"ERROR_NUMBER\\\"]  = \\\"0\\\"\\n```\\n\\nIn practice, any Java object can be stored in a context field — strings, numbers, collections, custom objects. The formatter tags define how those objects are serialized to/from XML.\\n\\n### Context Inheritance Chain\\n\\nContexts form an inheritance hierarchy via the `parent` attribute:\\n\\n```xml\\n<context id=\\\"BaseOpCtxt\\\"     parent=\\\"nil\\\"         type=\\\"op\\\"/>\\n<context id=\\\"InternetCtxt\\\"   parent=\\\"BaseOpCtxt\\\"  type=\\\"op\\\"/>\\n<context id=\\\"GetLinksCtxt\\\"   parent=\\\"InternetCtxt\\\" type=\\\"op\\\"/>\\n```\\n\\nWhen `GetLinksCtxt` is active:\\n- An opStep or formatter can read/write fields in `GetLinksCtxt`\\n- It can also read/write fields in `InternetCtxt` (parent)\\n- It can also read/write fields in `BaseOpCtxt` (grandparent)\\n- Each context has its **own isolated namespace** — there is no collision between field names in different levels\\n- Access traverses up the chain: if a field is not found in the current context, the runtime looks in the parent, then grandparent, up to `nil`\\n\\n### Context Access Rules\\n\\n- **Formatters** (CCString, CCDate, CCXML, etc.): read from and write to context fields identified by their `dataName` attribute\\n- **opStep implClasses**: have full access to the context chain — can read any field and write any field at any level they have access to\\n- **Decorators**: do NOT directly access context — they receive a string value from the formatter and return a transformed string\\n- **No component can access context fields from a sibling context** — only from its own context and its ancestors\\n\\n### Context in the Operation XML\\n\\n```xml\\n<context id=\\\"GetLinksCtxt\\\" parent=\\\"nil\\\" type=\\\"op\\\"/>\\n\\n<CCDSEServerOperation id=\\\"GetLinksOp\\\" operationContext=\\\"GetLinksCtxt\\\">\\n    ...\\n</CCDSEServerOperation>\\n```\\n\\nThe `operationContext` attribute binds the operation to its context. The context is instantiated once when the operation starts and lives until the operation completes.\\n\\n---\", \"content_hash\": \"37f170488586f0f792209cd78d6f595dd1f87d9fdf777e36a9b334bed6a2cec8\"}, {\"document\": \"embedded:composer_conversion_knowledge\", \"heading\": \"6. Formats and the Format/Unformat Process\", \"content\": \"## 6. Formats and the Format/Unformat Process\\n\\n### What a Format Is\\n\\nA `fmtDef` is a declarative description of an XML data structure. It is not a DTO class — it is a recursive tree of formatter tags, each of which knows how to:\\n- **unformat**: read its value from incoming XML and write it to the context\\n- **format**: read its value from context and write it to the output XML\\n\\nThe format tree is walked recursively. Each node in the tree is a formatter tag instance.\\n\\n### Format and Unformat Direction\\n\\n**Unformat (parsing — XML → context):**\\n```\\nIncoming XML string\\n  → root formatter tag's unformat() is called\\n  → root tag parses its children recursively\\n  → each leaf formatter reads its XML element value\\n  → (if decorators present: removeDecoration() chain applied first)\\n  → final value written to context[dataName]\\n```\\n\\n**Format (serializing — context → XML):**\\n```\\ncontext[dataName] value\\n  → (if decorators present: addDecoration() chain applied first)\\n  → leaf formatter writes its value as an XML element\\n  → parent formatters build the XML structure up the tree\\n  → result is the complete XML output string\\n```\\n\\n### Decorator Chain Direction\\n\\n**During unformat (parsing incoming XML):**\\n```\\nXML string value\\n  → last decorator in chain: removeDecoration(value)\\n  → second-to-last decorator: removeDecoration(previous result)\\n  → ... (chain runs in reverse order)\\n  → first decorator: removeDecoration(...)\\n  → result passed to formatter for context write\\n```\\n\\n**During format (building outgoing XML):**\\n```\\ncontext value (string from formatter)\\n  → first decorator in chain: addDecoration(value)\\n  → second decorator: addDecoration(previous result)\\n  → ... (chain runs in forward order)\\n  → last decorator: addDecoration(...)\\n  → result written to XML output\\n```\\n\\nThe decorator chain is defined by the order of decorator tags after the formatter tag in the XML.\\n\\n### Format Execution Contexts\\n\\nThe format/unformat process is not limited to request/response. It occurs whenever data needs to be serialized or deserialized:\\n\\n- **Request reception**: channel handler calls unformat on `csRequestFormat`\\n- **Response building**: channel handler calls format on `csReplyFormat` (or `csErrorReplyFormat` if error body was switched)\\n- **Backend request**: an opStep builds a request to a backend system using a format\\n- **Backend response**: an opStep parses a response from a backend system using a format\\n- **Logging**: some opSteps serialize context data to log using a format\\n\\n### refFormat — Format Reuse\\n\\n```xml\\n<!-- In CCDSEServerOperation: -->\\n<refFormat name=\\\"csRequestFormat\\\"  refid=\\\"GetLinksRQFmt\\\"/>\\n<refFormat name=\\\"csReplyFormat\\\"    refid=\\\"GetLinksRSFmt\\\"/>\\n<refFormat name=\\\"csErrorReplyFormat\\\" refid=\\\"StandardErrorFmt\\\"/>\\n```\\n\\nThe `name` attribute is the role the format plays in this operation. The conventional names are:\\n- `csRequestFormat` — the incoming request XML structure\\n- `csReplyFormat` — the success response XML structure\\n- `csErrorReplyFormat` — the error response XML structure (substituted when an opStep signals an error body change via `on{RC}Return`)\\n\\nThe `refid` points to a `fmtDef` id, which may be defined in the same XML file, in `dseformat.xml`, or in any other file loaded via `defaultFile`.\\n\\n### CCTableFormat — Database Lookup During Format\\n\\n`CCTableFormat` is a special formatter that performs a database lookup during the format process. When the format tree reaches a `CCTableFormat` node during format (building outgoing XML):\\n1. It reads the key value from context (identified by `keyValue` attribute)\\n2. Queries `fromTable` column `fromColumn` where the key matches\\n3. Writes the result as the field's XML value\\n\\nThis means database calls can happen during response building, not just during opStep execution.\\n\\n---\", \"content_hash\": \"8a0189fb3052b2fd2255f282277a4446377b592483378da3f02c0ffca162826c\"}, {\"document\": \"embedded:composer_conversion_knowledge\", \"heading\": \"7. Decorators\", \"content\": \"## 7. Decorators\\n\\n### What a Decorator Is\\n\\nA decorator is a value transformer chained after a formatter tag. It operates on the string result of the formatter, not on the context directly.\\n\\n**XML syntax:**\\n```xml\\n<CCString dataName=\\\"AccountId\\\"/>\\n<CCPadding padChar=\\\"0\\\" length=\\\"9\\\"/>\\n```\\n\\n`CCPadding` is a decorator that follows `CCString`. The decorator tag appears as a sibling immediately after the formatter's self-closing tag.\\n\\n### Decorator Contracts\\n\\nThere are two decorator base classes with different contracts:\\n\\n**Type 1 — Value Decorator** (extends `FormatDecoratorHolder`):\\n```java\\npublic String addDecoration(String s);     // called during FORMAT\\npublic String removeDecoration(String s);  // called during UNFORMAT\\npublic Object initializeFrom(Tag tag);     // reads this tag's own attributes\\n```\\n\\nExample — `CCPadding`:\\n- `addDecoration(\\\"1234567\\\")` → `\\\"001234567\\\"` (pad to length 9 with '0')\\n- `removeDecoration(\\\"001234567\\\")` → `\\\"1234567\\\"` (strip leading zeros)\\n\\n**Type 2 — Attribute Decorator** (extends `AttributeXmlFormatDecoratorImpl`):\\n```java\\npublic Hashtable formatXmlAttributes(Context ctx, DataElement de, FormatElement fe);\\npublic Object initializeFrom(Tag tag);\\n```\\n\\nThis type operates at the XML attribute level rather than the string value level. It can add XML attributes (like `xsi:nil=\\\"true\\\"`) to the output element. Example: `NilDecorator`.\\n\\n### Decorator Chain Rules\\n\\n1. A decorator applies only to the immediately preceding formatter tag\\n2. Multiple decorators can be chained after one formatter — each receives the previous one's output\\n3. During **format**: chain runs in order (first decorator → last decorator)\\n4. During **unformat**: chain runs in reverse order (last decorator → first decorator)\\n5. `initializeFrom(Tag tag)` reads only this decorator's own XML attributes — never the formatter's attributes or sibling tags\\n6. A decorator can be placed after a complex formatter (like `CCXML`) — in that case it decorates the entire XML subtree produced by that formatter\\n\\n### Example — Multiple Decorators\\n\\n```xml\\n<CCString dataName=\\\"Amount\\\"/>\\n<RemoveLeadingZerosDecorator/>\\n<CCPadding padChar=\\\" \\\" length=\\\"12\\\"/>\\n```\\n\\n**During unformat** (input XML: `<Amount>   0001234</Amount>`):\\n1. `CCPadding.removeDecoration(\\\"   0001234\\\")` → strips right-padding → `\\\"0001234\\\"`\\n2. `RemoveLeadingZerosDecorator.removeDecoration(\\\"0001234\\\")` → `\\\"1234\\\"`\\n3. `CCString` writes `\\\"1234\\\"` to context[\\\"Amount\\\"]\\n\\n**During format** (context[\\\"Amount\\\"] = \\\"1234\\\"):\\n1. `CCString` reads `\\\"1234\\\"` from context\\n2. `RemoveLeadingZerosDecorator.addDecoration(\\\"1234\\\")` → (no-op in format) → `\\\"1234\\\"`\\n3. `CCPadding.addDecoration(\\\"1234\\\")` → `\\\"        1234\\\"` (12 chars, space-padded left)\\n4. XML output: `<Amount>        1234</Amount>`\\n\\n### All Decorator Tags (from XML channel dse.ini)\\n\\n| Tag | Class | Description |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `nilDecorator` | `...decorator.NilDecorator` | Sets `xsi:nil=\\\"true\\\"` when value is null/empty |\\n| `RemoveLeadingZerosDecorator` | `...decorator.RemoveLeadingZerosDecorator` | Strips leading zeros |\\n| `CCPadding` | `...decorator.CCPadding` | Pads string to fixed length |\\n| `CCFixedLength` | `...decorator.CCFixedLength` | Enforces fixed string length |\\n| `CCMandatory` | `...decorator.CCMandatory` | Validates field is not empty |\\n| `CCNotNull` | `...decorator.CCNotNull` | Validates field is not null |\\n| `CCZeroToNull` | `...decorator.CCZeroToNull` | Converts zero value to null |\\n| `CCNullToZero` | `...decorator.CCNullToZero` | Converts null to zero |\\n| `fZeroToDecimalIDB` | `...decorator.ZeroToDecimalIDB` | Handles zero decimal display |\\n| `fFixedLengthTranIDB` | `...decorator.FixedLengthTranIDB` | Fixed-length transform |\\n| `fStringDateIDB` | `...decorator.StringDateIDB` | String-to-date conversion |\\n| `fZeroToNullIDB` | `...decorator.ZeroToNullIDB` | Zero-to-null for IDB |\\n| `fTrimIDB` | `...decorator.TrimIDB` | Trim whitespace for IDB |\\n| `SmartMirror` | `...decorator.SmartMirror` | Hebrew/Latin text mirroring |\\n| `HebrewWHF` | `...decorator.HebrewWHF` | Hebrew character handling |\\n| `MF2Hebrew` | `...decorator.MF2Hebrew` | Mainframe-to-Hebrew conversion |\\n| `Base64Decorator` | `...decorator.Base64Decorator` | Base64 encode/decode |\\n| `ArithmaticAction` | `...decorator.ArithmaticAction` | Arithmetic on value |\\n| `CCRegExp` | `...decorator.CCRegExp` | Regex validation |\\n| `CCRegExpReplace` | `...decorator.CCRegExpReplace` | Regex replace |\\n| `MaskLogDecorator` | `...decorator.MaskLogDecorator` | Masks value in logs |\\n| `TypeReceive` | `...decorator.TypeReceive` | Type conversion on receive |\\n| `SetCenturyFor2DigitsYear` | `...decorator.SetCenturyFor2DigitsYear` | Y2K year handling |\\n| `CCPhoneNumberDecorator` | `...decorator.CCPhoneNumberDecorator` | Phone number formatting |\\n| `AltamiraChannelDecorator` | `...decorator.AltamiraChannelDecorator` | Altamira channel transform |\\n| `HebrewLogicalToVisualDecorator` | `...decorator.HebrewLogicalToVisualDecorator` | Hebrew visual order |\\n| `unicodeDecorator` | `...decorator.UnicodeDecorator` | Unicode handling |\\n| `convertReservedTags` | `...decorator.ConvertReservedTags` | XML reserved char escaping |\\n| `delimS` | `...decorator.DelimiterStr` | Delimiter-based splitting |\\n\\n---\", \"content_hash\": \"0dae02d0709a670195856f35ecba11496c6e6987d38f2be86dd13838877833fd\"}]}"}],"role":"user"}],"config":{"system_instruction":"Mandatory target-code contract for the FIRST response and every correction:\nGenerate ordinary native Java business behavior, not a Composer compatibility runtime.\nAll original XML, Java source and embedded Composer documentation are behavior evidence\nONLY, including their imports and code examples. They are not reusable target APIs.\nNo com.ibm imports or executable references in ANY generated main or test file. Do not\ncopy or rename Context, format/decorator holders, Tag initialization or framework engines.\nUse explicit typed inputs/results and plain mapper transformations for decorators.\nReuse supplied accepted native interfaces without changing them. Retain documented ordinary\nexternal dependencies where required; do not invent replacement business behavior.\nReuse known_dependencies coordinates, versions and scopes exactly for EVERY known artifact.\nDo not choose new versions for known libraries. Declare only dependencies used by the returned\nmain/test code; keep required_classes tied to those imports. Propose a new pinned dependency\nonly when its artifact is absent from known_dependencies and genuinely needed.\nUse the supplied current JUnit Jupiter dependency for generated JUnit 5 tests; include it in\ndependencies with its current scope (normally scope test). When JUnit is not known, the\napproved test dependency below is the fallback, not an override of existing dependencies. Test and Assertions belong to junit-jupiter-api, supplied\ntransitively by junit-jupiter. The engine executes tests; it is not the API containing\nTest/Assertions. required_classes lists actual imported APIs, including test imports.\nKeep all other dependency coordinates pinned and justified by generated code.\nReturn exactly one JSON object matching the supplied schema, with no prose or fences.\nEvery file path starts with src/main/java/ or src/test/java/, followed by its package\npath and public type filename. Never return package-relative paths without these prefixes.\nBefore returning EVERY response, check valid JSON syntax and escaped Java strings; verify\nunit_contract method metadata matches the actual public Java methods, all imported APIs\nhave dependencies, and coverage maps every supplied requirement to executable test files.\nThe example below illustrates response structure and native code style ONLY: adapt its\npackage, unit ID, evidence IDs, requirements, classes and behavior to the current evidence;\nnever copy its sample behavior into the real unit. The supplied schema is authoritative.\n\nApproved test dependency:\n{\"group_id\": \"org.junit.jupiter\", \"artifact_id\": \"junit-jupiter\", \"version\": \"5.10.0\", \"scope\": \"test\", \"reason\": \"JUnit Jupiter tests and execution engine\", \"required_classes\": [\"org.junit.jupiter.api.Test\", \"org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions\"]}\nCorrect response example:\n{\"files\": [{\"path\": \"src/main/java/com/company/generated/example/BusinessStep.java\", \"content\": \"package com.company.generated.example; public class BusinessStep { public String execute(String value) { return value; } }\"}, {\"path\": \"src/test/java/com/company/generated/example/BusinessStepTest.java\", \"content\": \"package com.company.generated.example; import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test; import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals; public class BusinessStepTest { @Test public void preservesValue() { assertEquals(\\\"value\\\", new BusinessStep().execute(\\\"value\\\")); } }\"}], \"dependencies\": [{\"group_id\": \"org.junit.jupiter\", \"artifact_id\": \"junit-jupiter\", \"version\": \"5.10.0\", \"scope\": \"test\", \"reason\": \"JUnit Jupiter tests and execution engine\", \"required_classes\": [\"org.junit.jupiter.api.Test\", \"org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions\"]}], \"coverage\": {\"business\": [\"src/test/java/com/company/generated/example/BusinessStepTest.java\"]}, \"evidence_ids\": [\"example-source\"], \"unresolved_questions\": [], \"input_type\": \"java.lang.String\", \"output_type\": \"java.lang.String\", \"unit_contract\": {\"unit_id\": \"example-unit\", \"apis\": [{\"type_name\": \"com.company.generated.example.BusinessStep\", \"method_signatures\": [\"public java.lang.String execute(java.lang.String)\"]}], \"dependency_units\": [], \"requirements\": {\"business\": \"Preserve the evidenced value\"}, \"evidence_ids\": [\"example-source\"]}, \"schema_version\": \"v1\"}\nUnit-specific instructions:\nReturn unit_contract with this unit_id, exact fully qualified public APIs matching the returned files, requirements and evidence_ids. Include input_type, output_type and wire_type where applicable. Generate typed data classes needed by this unit in the same bundle. dependency_units may name only supplied accepted units. Use the assigned native_package.\nImplement one configured business step with the native APIs you declare in this response.\nUse original implementation/helper source and XML attributes as behavior evidence. Replace\ncontext access with typed arguments/results and replace Composer inheritance and service\nlookup with declared collaborators. Merge small helpers where appropriate; retain database\nand HTTP integration interfaces where required. Preserve calculations, return outcomes,\nexceptions, configured values and side-effect order. Routing is owned by the enclosing service.\nReuse accepted dependency APIs without redefining them.\nInclude native companion implementations for supporting behavior required by this step\nwhen it is not provided by a supplied accepted native API or a retained, declared ordinary\nexternal dependency. Read the supporting source evidence and implement its required behavior\nin this bundle, including integration collaborators and their helpers. Declare and wire\nevery generated collaborator consistently in implementation code, public API metadata and\ntests. An interface or mock alone does not implement a required production collaborator.\nDo not assume an original helper has already been migrated, invent a target package for it,\nor fix a missing helper by importing its IBM source class. Before returning, check that\nevery required supporting type resolves to a returned native file, an accepted dependency\nAPI or a declared ordinary library. Preserve unknowns explicitly rather than inventing behavior.\nReturn one valid JSON bundle matching schema, with main files and executable test files.\ncoverage maps every requirement ID to test file paths. Tests must check evidenced behavior\nand side effects. Include evidence_ids and unresolved_questions; do not implement invented\ndefaults for unknown production behavior. Address correction_feedback, behavior_review_feedback and final_validation_feedback without changing the\napproved interfaces. No Composer Context/router/formatter classes, TODOs, fences or POMs.\nConfigured Java target: Java 25. All generated implementation code, test code, and proposed dependencies must support Java 25. Tests must compile and execute on Java 25. Do not assume a testing library is compatible merely because it resolves or compiles. Preserve existing dependency versions and scopes. If they prevent compatibility with the configured Java target, report the conflict in unresolved_questions instead of silently upgrading them or generating incomplete replacements.\nFollow the versioned testing_contract, its pinned dependencies and reference examples. Keep tests focused, separate business and adapter tests, and mock external interfaces instead of hand implementing them. Example values are illustrative only; derive assertions from the original evidence.\nWhen compiler_correction is supplied, correct the latest failed_sources using\nits diagnostics and relevant_dependency_apis. Check every replacement call's parameters and\nreturn type against the verified API. Do not invent methods or change accepted interfaces.\nFor a missing supporting class or package, check the returned files, supplied accepted native\nAPIs and retained declared dependencies. When supporting source evidence defines required\nbehavior with no available native implementation, include that companion implementation in\nthe corrected bundle and wire its callers, metadata and tests to it. Merely changing the\nimport, restoring the IBM class or adding only an interface/mock is not a production fix.\nPreserve evidenced business behavior and working code; implement behavior locally only when\nthe original evidence supports it. Compiler diagnostics identify invalid code, not a business\nreplacement. Keep the original compiler output as supporting evidence and return the complete\ncorrected bundle, including matching metadata and tests, in the required JSON schema.\nWhen test_correction is supplied, compare its failing test, setup,\nassertion, exception and latest implementation sources against the original source evidence\nand configuration in this request. Actual and expected values are observations when available,\nnot proof that the test expectation is correct. Determine whether the test, implementation or\nboth disagree with the evidence. Correct the mismatch without weakening assertions, dropping\nbehavior coverage or changing unrelated behavior or accepted APIs. Preserve passing cases and\nreturn the complete corrected bundle and matching metadata; the full test suite will rerun.\nHonor every versioned_requirements ID and version. Provide executable coverage for the meaningful behavior obligations in requirements; one focused test may cover multiple source files. DTOs, getters, configuration and forwarding helpers do not each need separate tests when their behavior is exercised through mapper, workflow or caller tests. The testing_contract platform policy is validated directly through dependencies, source safeguards and the build; do not add a platform coverage entry or declare it in unit_contract.requirements. Changing metadata alone does not satisfy a changed behavior requirement.\nReturn actual JSON syntax, not JSON encoded inside JSON. dependencies must be an array of objects with quoted keys. Use real whitespace between JSON tokens; never write literal backslash-n or escaped quote delimiters outside JSON strings. Escape newlines and quotes only inside string values such as Java source. Before returning every response (initial or correction), check the entire response for valid JSON syntax and verify it against schema.\n\nYou are an agent. Your internal name is \"MigrationRuntime\"."},"live_connect_config":{"input_audio_transcription":{},"output_audio_transcription":{}}}
